  "rationale": "The added columns target the query well in principle: a performance tier and an achievement gap give genuine axes to identify top performers and quantify improvement. However improvement_potential is a trivial per-category constant that merely restates performance_category and fabricates specific improvement numbers unsupported by the text, and target_alignment largely duplicates the performance/gap signal. Groundedness is moderate: category and gap are derivable from existing target/percent_complete columns, but the sampled values show internal inconsistencies (e.g. 'Strong Performer' with a -27 gap, 'Underperformer' with a 61+ gap) and the invented improvement constants, indicating several values are not sound readings of the source."
